      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Over-the-counter pain medications like acetaminophen (Tylenol) or ibuprofen (Advil) may help alleviate fever and pain, but please consult your doctor first to confirm they are safe for your specific situation. Avoid taking ibuprofen for the first 7-10 days after surgery as it can increase bleeding risk. You can also try gentle heat or cold packs to soothe the area, but avoid using them for extended periods or if you have any concerns.",
      "source": "target",
